{
  "Lets users reorder items by dragging them with the pointer or a finger, or with the keyboard. Lists in the same group can exchange items. A drop moves the element and reports the indexes, while your data stays under your control.": "",
  "Using children as items": "",
  "JSX children are the items. Drag one, or focus it and press Ctrl + Down. `onReorder` reports the old and new positions, and the application reorders its own data.": "",
  "Binding to data and moving between lists": "",
  "`items` with an `itemTemplate` renders rows from your data and keeps each row when the order changes. Two sortables in the same `group` can exchange items. `onRemove` and `onAdd` notify both sides, and each list redraws its array.": "",
  "Drag handles, horizontal lists and canceling a drag": "",
  "A drag starts after a few pixels with the pointer, or after a long press with a finger (a finger that moves first scrolls). A copy follows the pointer, the item stays faded in place, and a line shows the drop position. The list scrolls near its edges.": "",
  "The item's element moves there immediately, and `onReorder` reports the old and new positions. Your code reorders the data. Between sortables in a group, `onRemove` and `onAdd` report the same to both sides.": "",
  "With `items`, each item keeps its component when the order changes, because rows are keyed by item. Reordering your array moves the rows without recreating them.": "",
  "The focused item, or its handle if it has one, responds to Ctrl + Up and Down (Left and Right when horizontal) and Ctrl + Home and End. Each move is reported to `onReorder` and announced.": "",
  "Cancels a drag, and nothing moves.": "",
  "A `group` named by `label`. The items are whatever you put in it.": "",
  "One Tab stop that moves between items with the keyboard. An item with its own focusable element keeps it. A handle is a button that you name.": "",
  "Each keyboard move is announced: “Moved to 2 of 5”.": "",
  "The list. `data-orientation`, `data-sortable`, and `data-drop-target` while a dragged item can land here.": "",
  "Each item. `data-dragging` on the item being dragged.": "",
  "The drop indicator line.": "",
  "The copy that follows the pointer.": "",
  "Units: the list (`target`), an item (`sortable`, `dragging`, `focus`), the line (its thickness and color, vertical in a horizontal list), and the copy.": "",
  "The gap between items.": "",
  "The items, each drawn with `itemTemplate`. Without them, the JSX children are the items.": "",
  "The item text": "",
  "Creates the component for an item. Because it is a function, it is not bound like the other props.": "",
  "A selector inside an item for the part that handles dragging and the keyboard. Without it, the whole item does.": "",
  "Sortables in the same group can exchange items.": "",
  "Allows items to be moved. `false` keeps them in place.": "",
  "`vertical` or `horizontal`. The drop line and the move keys follow it.": "",
  "The accessible name of the list.": "",
  "Occurs before a drag or keyboard move starts (`item`, `fromIndex`). Set `cancel = true` to prevent it.": "",
  "Occurs when the drop position changes (`to`, `toIndex`). Set `cancel = true` to reject that position.": "",
  "Occurs before the drop. Set `cancel = true` to leave everything unchanged.": "",
  "Occurs when an item moves within this sortable (`fromIndex`, `toIndex`, `item`), by a drop or the keyboard. Reorder your data here.": "",
  "Occur when an item leaves for another sortable in the group and when it arrives, with `from`, `to`, the indexes and the item. Move the data between your arrays here.": "",
  "Moves an item programmatically as a drop would, and raises `onReorder`.": "",
  "The item elements, in order.": "",
  "Indicates that an item is being dragged.": ""
